    host: conn.host,           // e.g. "db.internal"
    migrations: migrationFiles, // filenames only
  };
  // POST payload to the audit endpoint over HTTPS...
}
```

This gives a real compliance trail (what ran, where, when) without putting passwords or API keys on the network. If you want, I can wire that up — and if the audit service genuinely needs to authenticate the request, the right approach is a dedicated audit API token sent in an `Authorization` header, not the database/cloud secrets themselves.

